I haven't fully thought through scoping in advance.

But my intuition is that top-level things go into one scope, then each top-level thing
has its own internal scope.

I think I am aiming for a Miranda/Haskell/FLAS-like "scope is upward visibility" mechanism.

So here we define two targets, each with a variable called "tmp".  They are separate,
and each one should work with its own environment.

	target the_first
		env "HELLO" => tmp
		show tmp

	target the_second
		env "GOODBYE" => tmp
		show tmp